{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"AWS Lambda now supports Java 8, 11, and 17 on Amazon Linux 2023 - AWS","context":"AWS Lambda now supports Java 8, 11, and 17 runtimes on Amazon Linux 2023 (AL2023), available as managed runtimes and container base images. This update enables customers to migrate from Amazon Linux 2 without requiring a Java version upgrade. The existing Lambda runtimes for Java 8, 11, and 17 on AL2, which reached end of life on June 30, 2026, will remain supported until June 30, 2027, with patches for critical and selected important security issues. AWS recommends upgrading to Java 21 or Java 25 on AL2023 for the latest language features and performance improvements. The Java 8, 11, and 17 runtimes on AL2023 are available in all AWS Regions where Lambda is available, including AWS GovCloud (US) and China Regions. Customers can use AWS Transform custom to assist with the migration to Java 21 or Java 25. The Java 8, 11, and 17 runtimes on AL2023 provide an alternative forward path for those not yet ready to upgrade their Java version","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/aws-lambda-java-amazon-linux/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"AWS Lambda adds support for Python 3.13 - AWS","context":"AWS Lambda has added support for Python 3.13 as both a managed runtime and a container base image. This latest LTS release of Python is expected to be supported until October 2029. Python 3.13 can be used with Lambda@Edge in supported regions, allowing for customization of low-latency content delivered through Amazon CloudFront. Powertools for AWS Lambda, a developer toolkit, also supports Python 3.13","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2024/11/aws-lambda-support-python-313/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"AWS Lambda adds support for Python 3.14 - AWS","context":"AWS Lambda has added support for Python 3.14 as both a managed runtime and a container base image. Developers can utilize the latest Python 3.14 language features with Lambda and Lambda@Edge in supported Regions. Powertools for AWS Lambda, a developer toolkit, also supports Python 3.14. AWS provides various deployment tools, including the Lambda console, AWS CLI, AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM), AWS CDK, and AWS CloudFormation, to deploy and manage serverless applications written in Python 3.14. The Python 3.14 runtime is available in all AWS Regions, including AWS GovCloud (US) and China Regions. For more information on upgrading existing Lambda functions and other details, refer to the blog post and AWS Lambda product page","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2025/11/aws-lambda-python-314/"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"aws-lambda-durable-functions","skill_description":"Builds resilient, long-running, multi-step applications with AWS Lambda durable functions with automatic state persistence, retry logic, and orchestration for long-running executions. Covers the critical replay model, step operations, wait/callback patterns, error handling with saga pattern, testing with LocalDurableTestRunner. Triggers on phrases like lambda durable functions, durable execution, workflow orchestration, state machines, retry/checkpoint patterns, long-running stateful Lambda functions, saga pattern, human-in-the-loop callbacks, reliable serverless applications, context.step, context.wait, context.invoke, context.runInChildContext, withDurableExecution, DurableContext, UnrecoverableInvocationError, durable-execution-sdk, qualified ARN invocation, and durable handler replay.\n\nServices: lambda\nTasks: deploy, debug, operate\nPersona: developer\nWorkload: serverless, compute","skill_name":"aws-lambda-durable-functions"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"debugging-lambda-timeouts","skill_description":"Debugs AWS Lambda function timeout failures by systematically analyzing function configuration, CloudWatch logs and metrics, VPC/networking, cold starts, memory constraints, and downstream dependencies to identify root causes with actionable fixes. Use when a Lambda function is timing out or approaching its timeout limit.\n\nServices: lambda, cloudwatch, vpc, rds, dynamodb, iam\nTasks: debug, troubleshoot\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: serverless","skill_name":"debugging-lambda-timeouts"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Verify Lambda Python 3.9 runtime deprecation/end-of-support date", "parent_id": "3d3ae6d7-dfd8-4ad4-a49c-4504a0a101a3"}
